Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-17-2001||10:13 AM||||Late for work this morning.. went over a blind hill.... met a ghost car! - and the lights went on....<P>Caught for doing 130km in a 90 km area..(80mph in a 55 mph)<P>The Woman Officer who stopped me asked if I know why I was stopped..   I told her I was speeding.. I also mentioned I was late for work and that's the reason I was speeding..<P>After sitting there waiting in my car while she was in hers filling out the papers, She came back and gave me a WARNING tiket!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>she said to keep the speed down because I wont make it to work if i'm in the ditch.<P>She must have been having a good morning..she was smiling the whole time..<P>I'm smiling also after that too.. Sure beats having a huge fine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||overlord||06-17-2001||10:56 AM||||sweet.<BR>she didnt happen to leave her phone number on the warning did she?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-17-2001||11:11 AM||||nope  lol<P>but she was sure friendly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||06-17-2001||12:23 PM||||You bastard!!  I was going the same over (I was 24 over, not 25 like you).  Anyway, I was going 64 in a 40, and I got a ticket for 64 in a 40.  My guy wasn't a nice one.  He asked if I was late for school (after lunch), and I said yeah, and he said:  "Well, you're going to be even later."  Damn.  $97.  Or in your case, $800 CAN.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||06-17-2001||07:02 PM||||Not that this will work for evey officer or every stop, but, I have let people go who have sirred me to death, been apologetic and answered every question truthfully,ie. "I was going **mph" and their speed is what I had them at or they admit to what they did wrong. <P>You've got to remember, we get lied to alot, everyone will try to make themselves look better by not quite telling the truth. <P>When someone comes along who is totally 100% honest it can, and has with me, made a difference.<P>That's just my take on things, now rag about me, it'll make ya feel better.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||06-17-2001||07:33 PM||||You know something this PISSES ME OFF!! I have only ever gotten ONE TICKET, in my fiero 145KLM/HR in an 100... while late for work in the 427 in Toronto, stupid women cop wouldn't do anything asked me why I said I was late.  She said "Gosh you are REALLY gonna be late now eh?"  then she handed me the ticket, and I asked if we could work something out, she said "Yep come to court and try to reduce it, but I do'nt reduce tickets for young punks driving sports cars you are all inconsiderate and dangerous"<P>So I fought it anyway and got it reduced to 110 (Saves the insurance!)<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||06-17-2001||07:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Not that this will work for evey officer or every stop, but, I have let people go who have sirred me to death, been apologetic and answered every question truthfully,ie. "I was going **mph" and their speed is what I had them at or they admit to what they did wrong. <P>You've got to remember, we get lied to alot, everyone will try to make themselves look better by not quite telling the truth. <P>When someone comes along who is totally 100% honest it can, and has with me, made a difference.<P>That's just my take on things, now rag about me, it'll make ya feel better.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I definietly agree with that.  The few times I have been pulled over (Going through a no turn on red, and speeding on a beach access road on my way to work 53 in a 25  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ), I have always said "sir" and have always been totally honest and cooperative with the officer.  I have gone away with warnings each time.  But I know eventually I will one day get a ticket, and I will be nice about it.  btw, this is coming from a Criminal Justice Major, so I guess I just like to traet officers with the respect that I would like to be treated with.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Galen||06-17-2001||08:08 PM||||Only got stopped for speeding once, got seatbelt tickets twice but we wont go there, it was like 11:30 at night and I had sped up a lil 55 in a 45 and saw a cop in front of me, was about to slow down and turn and pop, bluelights from behind me. was a nice cop, told me to promise him I'd be careful and he'd let me go. sounded like a good deal to me..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
